    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (76.32) and **Daulton Varsho** (72.31) anchor our lineup as the premier plays. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a favorable matchup against Rodriguez, whose 4.57 xERA provides a ceiling-raising environment for our 3B. Similarly, **Daulton Varsho** is a high-upside start against Rodr\u00edguez, who carries a shaky 5.91 xERA; the combination of a positive park factor and a significant platoon advantage against the right-hander makes him an essential piece of our outfield today. **Jonathan Aranda** (69.13) also projects as an elite start, as he faces a soft matchup against Melton, with the platoon advantage contributing a massive 12-point boost to his base projection.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Justin Crawford** (45.13). While his speed profile is highly coveted, he narrowly missed the cut due to a combination of a tough matchup against Woo and a bottom-of-the-order assignment that suppressed his counting stat projection compared to the consistency of **Gavin Sheets** (57.25) and **Dylan Beavers** (58.19). Elsewhere, **Zack Gelof** (61.03) warrants a close watch; while his power/speed profile is strong, he is facing a sub-4.00 xERA arm in Prielipp, though his 10% park boost keeps him firmly in the \"Strong\" start tier. We are navigating these matchups carefully to balance our daily efficiency against the reality that **Will Smith** remains unavailable on the IL, placing additional pressure on **Cal Raleigh** (49.37) to deliver productivity from the catcher slot against a formidable arm in Luzardo.",
